# netsurf: items in or out of a block-level flex box are placed alone (patch 502)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 501)
#
# A child-list change on a flex or grid box with boxed children in or out
# built the whole box again (patches 438/439, html_rl_flex_whole:
# "a flex or grid box's child list changed in elements with a box"). On
# stackoverflow.com, script inserts into large flex containers rebuilt
# ~1,400 elements each time, ~90-200 ms per insert in the simulator,
# ~0.6 s of a 5.2 s load's main thread.
#
# html_rl_block_change now places the items as it places blocks -- each
# new one built alone (box_build_element) and linked after its earlier
# sibling's box, removed ones unlinked -- and lays the page out whole,
# when the placement is the plain one: a block-level BOX_FLEX with no
# object, control, frame or marker; every child box under it an
# element's (an implied flex item, i.e. a run of inline content, is
# "more than blocks" and falls back, so no line can be split or joined);
# no non-space text; an element child that keeps its box (its own :empty
# cannot change). The leaf, inline, late and float placements are
# skipped in this mode (such a new element falls back), and an item built
# anywhere but straight under the flex box is a full reconvert, as the
# block path's own surprises are. The structural (:nth-child) and
# sibling-rule checks run as for blocks: matching siblings restyled
# alone, or the box built again whole. Grid, inline-flex and the rest
# keep the whole rebuild.
#
# Gate: JS-flex-items / CSS-flex-items-ref (sixteen steps, row for row
# against the same steps at parse time).
